      "worked_solution": "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-2,2)$ and passes through the point $(7,5).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-2,2)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y-2)^{2}=4p(x+2).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(7,5),$ we substitute $x=7$ and $y=5$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5-2)^{2} & =4p(7+2) \\\\ 9 & =4p(9) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-2)^{2} & =(x+2) \\\\ 4 & =x+2 \\\\ x & =4-2 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $2.$",
